An unordered, forward-facing backlog; completed work and its rationale
live in the git history of this file, docs/plans/, docs/design/, and
NEWS.

Items are listed alphabetically by plan name; the order carries no
meaning. Most items have an implementation plan in docs/plans/<name>.md
(a few record instead in a design doc or a differently-named plan,
named in the item), and the planning/implementation/review process (who
plans, who implements, who reviews, which gates run) is
docs/plans/README.md.
No item is deferred to post-release, and gate labels (decision-gated,
consumer-gated) rank priority rather than block work (VD 2026-07-17).
Standing rule (VD 2026-08-06): gate an item IF we cannot think of
anything valuable it might enable - that failure, not the absence of
a caller today, is the only licensed gating fact. "consumer-gated"
below reads accordingly, and the gate lifts the moment a valuable
enabled model or use comes to mind. An existing consumer is
sufficient evidence of value, never necessary.

Standing fact (VD, 2026-07-06): single-chain n >= 1e5 workloads are
common. The large-n performance items are live, not consumer-gated.

Standing discipline (from the 2026-08-07 census, 65ef425): verify an
entry's status claims against git and live code before scoping from
it; re-run a full census before release. The 2026-08-08 value scan
(docs/design/model-space-survey.md sec 7) re-read every gated entry
under the enabling-value rule; its per-entry verdicts are folded into
the entries below.

items
  augmentation-helpers: exported R helpers for the augmentation draws
    dbarts already runs internally (Polya-Gamma, Albert-Chib,
    scale-mixture), so a host composing dbarts inside a larger
    Gibbs/MH sampler replicates them without re-deriving the math.
    Value-lifted by the r-c-division adoption slate
    (docs/design/r-c-division.md); ~240 lines. SCHEDULED, pre-release.
  bcf-public-surface: S0-S4 and S6 landed; the public creation
    surface exists (plan + landing notes in
    docs/plans/bcf-public-surface.md). REMAINING: S5 (bcf() and the
    bartBCF fit class) is PAUSED and RELOCATED to bartCause, per VD's
    extension-surface fork 4 (RESOLVED 2026-08-11: bartCause, on its
    dbarts-1.0 branch). The
    treatment=/moderators=/treatmentForest= names (and flat
    setTreatment/bcfGlue) are PROVISIONAL, scheduled for replacement
    by forests = list(forest(basis = ...)) per
    multiforest-extension-surface M2. Its S0 BCF transactional-
    setPredictor and per-observation-session pins
    (bcf-public-surface.md:326-327) are INVERTED IN PLACE by
    multiforest-predictor-mutation's S1 (the whole-matrix/column
    entries) and S2 (the two per-observation entries), in
    test-bcf-mutation-pins.R, test-bcf-r5-surface.R, and
    test-multi-forest-seam.R: each retirement commit edited the
    assertion this arc wrote from REFUSE to ACCEPT in place, rather
    than deleting or duplicating it.
  bcf-sigma-tail-mixing: OPTIONAL research door (docs/plans/bcf-sigma-
    residual.md sec 4 item 2; no separate plan doc). Open: the EXTREME
    tail (|a0| >= ~40, ~3% of the prior) is frozen-structure mixing
    that no amount of burn fixes; a principled remedy would target
    tree-structure mixing at high SNR (tempered early sweeps,
    restart-style grow proposals). Low priority - the regime only
    arises with a stale build scale swapped against a new response
    inside a larger Gibbs loop (setResponse updateScale=FALSE).
    research-open, decision-gated.
  blocked-jacobi-trees: RESEARCHED, KILLED 2026-07-21 (df13c04 +
    77597cc) - full record, lesson, and reopen clause in
    docs/plans/blocked-jacobi-trees.md and
    docs/design/within-chain-threading.md.
  cheap-uniformity: COMPLETE 2026-08-09 (S0-S4; plan + landing notes
    in docs/plans/cheap-uniformity.md). Sparse-valued mutation,
    per-column x.test update, and engine-resident sparse predict all
    open; the dbarts.h reshape mirrors this final surface.
  composition-validator: an SBC (simulation-based calibration) check
    over a user-supplied one-sweep closure, so a host composing
    dbarts inside a larger Gibbs/MH sampler can validate its own
    composition rather than trust it. Value-lifted by the
    r-c-division adoption slate: it is the item that catches the
    measured posterior-mean-as-draws defect class
    (docs/design/r-c-division.md). ~350 lines. SCHEDULED, pre-release.
  correlated-outcomes: multivariate/SUR outcomes SHIPPED as mvbart()
    in stan4bart with zero dbarts code (docs/design/correlated-
    outcomes.md). Open: AR-1 / serially-correlated errors
    (longitudinal, panel, ITS, DiD) compose today via a latent
    AR-state + nugget in the outer sampler (the rbart_vi pattern),
    with EXACT pure-AR-1 errors a deferred ENGINE door (banded
    residual precision + cross-leaf GLS leaf updates break per-leaf
    independence). causal-motivated, decision-gated.
  csc-code-validation: LANDED (record in
    docs/plans/csc-code-validation.md); categorical ingestion bounds
    codes against training-side K everywhere.
  empty-leaf-veto-fix: draw-law fix to the empty-leaf veto
