  multinomial-counts-mutation: multinomial BART cannot mutate its
    RESPONSE side - alone among the families it cannot serve as a
    conditional inside a larger Gibbs sampler. The response is the
    combiner-owned counts_ matrix, so the content is a new COUNTS and
    n x K OFFSET channel plus creation-side surface. Enables
    competing-risks discrete-time hazard (moves with
    survival-followups), nominal-response IRT and discrete choice,
    SUR-style composition past the multinomial boundary. The
    predictor channel is already open; the gap is response-side only.
    COMPLETE 2026-08-12 (S1-S5; plan + landing notes in
    docs/plans/multinomial-counts-mutation.md: S1 729bbdd counts
    channel, S2 d7d27a3 train category offset, S3 1027be5 test
