    slices S0-S2, AFTER the multiforest and multinomial arcs;
    consumer cost = five stan4bart call sites, others rebuild). The
    BCF-specific flat rename is a CARVE-OUT there (binding decision 3
    + S1 item 5b): setTreatment -> setForestBasis, bcfGlue ->
    numForestAmplitudes + forestAmplitudes. Extension-surface fork 3
    (the condition) is RESOLVED 2026-08-11 in favour of the rename;
    it lands at reshape S1. setData on a CSC/mixed store: SURVEYED,
    KEPT UNDESIGNED - no model surfaced (classes needing sparse
    designs do not swap whole data mid-chain; mid-chain mutation
    targets dense latent columns, which mixed containers carry).
    Per-observation mutation of CSC-backed columns stays a DOCUMENTED
    REFUSAL (O(nnz) shift, and no surveyed model needs it). The hot
    layer stays quantized codes + double cuts; response/offset/
    weights stay double*.
  variance-forest-mutation-routing: RESOLVED - the release-blocking
    memory-safety hole is closed and every heteroscedastic mutation
    entry routes the variance forest correctly or refuses cleanly
    (full record and landing notes in
    docs/plans/variance-forest-mutation-routing.md). The
    transactional/per-observation door CLOSED: it landed via
    multiforest-predictor-mutation S3 (a825263, 2026-08-12), which
    also CLOSED stateIsValid's variance OCCUPANCY gap in the same
    slice (open decision 1 took the variance forest IN rather than
    re-homing this item there). Doors still open, recorded there:
    scale-leaf staleness under updateScale; heteroscedastic
    prior-predictive draw; the setState variance COLUMN-MASK gap - a
    distinct, still-open check (columnMaskSubtreeIsValid has no
    variance-branch backstop), not the occupancy gap S3 closed.
  weighted-binary: integer-weight probit via replicated latents;
    arbitrary real weights need a real-shape PG sampler (IPW is a
    pseudo-likelihood trap; the approximate-PG decision is shared
    with negbin-real-dispersion). decision-gated.
  x86-simd: CLOSED as a perf lever - compute width is already emitted,
    and the remaining kernel candidates measured NO-GO (records in
    docs/plans/simd-flag-multiversioning.md, x86-simd.md,
    docs/design/memory-wall-frontier.md). The live perf frontier is
    the MEMORY WALL (frontier doc secs 10-13; the fused-suffstat arc
    landed from it). Remaining doors: weighted/fp32 fusion legs
    (would extend the fused path to BCF/multinomial/logistic through
    their weights), move-phase child gathers, K=8. All unmeasured;
    reopen with numbers.

release (deferred; the one ordered procedure, run when VD triggers it)
  note: the schedule/dispatch-only workflows (equivalence, rchk,
    revdep-smoke, sbc, valgrind) cannot register or run until they
    exist on the default branch - GitHub binds BOTH schedule and
    workflow_dispatch to it, so today they 404 even for a manual run.
    Their first live runs happen when bartcore merges to main;
    validate them then. rchk and valgrind have never run anywhere:
    macOS arm64 supports neither, so the merge is what buys the
    PROTECT-balance and memcheck passes CRAN itself runs. HELD
    2026-07-25 (VD): main stays as it is until VD's own review of the
    branch; revisit these checks then.
  the dbarts.h reshape lands BEFORE the freeze - the last planned
    pre-release breaking change; re-verify stan4bart bartcore against
    the reshaped header in the same window.
  push dbarts 1.0-0 (branch bartcore) and stan4bart 0.0-14; submit both
    to CRAN together. bartCause is ready and PUSHED on branch
    dbarts-1.0 in ~/Repositories/bartCause (ahead of its main; checks
    Status OK): submit it after dbarts is accepted.
  close GitHub issue #80 at release: fully resolved by the setResponse
    updateScale switch (cf70fd5; default FALSE locks the creation-time
    prior scale - the safe embedded-Gibbs behavior the issue asks for;
    latent families never rescale by construction). Point the reporter
    at the dbartsSampler-class.Rd and NEWS entries.
  on any post-release dbarts.h change: bump DBARTS_C_API_MINOR (or MAJOR
    if incompatible) alongside the hash re-bake, and bump stan4bart's
    Depends/LinkingTo dbarts floor in the same lockstep release - the
    load handshake covers the library-ahead direction, the floor covers
    consumer-ahead; both must move together.
  optional courtesy: notify the tmle maintainers. Their default
    SuperLearner dbarts wrappers pass obsWeights unconditionally and
    pnorm() the latents; unit weights are handled dbarts-side now, but
    genuinely weighted binomial analyses lose the dbarts learners by
    design, and family routing on their side would need the matching
    inverse link.
  at submission, re-run the FULL battery on the tip: R CMD check
    --as-cran on a clean-copy tarball, the suite, and the equivalence
    trio against the current baselines (the last full pre-submission
    gate run predates many engine commits; details in
    docs/plans/cran-readiness.md and this file's git history).
